  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Consider the following game featuring two fair six-sided dice rolled simultaneously. If the sum of the numbers on the dice is $6,$ the player wins $$6.$ Otherwise, the player loses $$1.$ What is the expected profit from each roll in this game? Round your answer to three decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single roll of the game. On each roll in the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- If the sum of the outcomes is $6$ ($(1,5),(2,4),(3,3),(4,2)$, or $(5,1)$), the player wins $$6,$ so we have $p=6.$\n\n- If the sum of the outcomes is not $6,$ the player loses $$1,$ so we have $p=-1.$\n\nThe probabilities for the outcomes are\n\n$$\nP(6)=\\frac{5}{36},\\,P(-1)=\\frac{31}{36}.\n$$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table. If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{5}{36}$ | $\\frac{31}{36}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $6$ | $-1$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[p] & =6\\cdot f(6)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{5}{36})+(-1)(\\frac{31}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{36}-\\frac{31}{36} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{36} \\\\  & \u2248-0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $-$0.028.$",
